e the 2 parts of complex numbers known as?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In a + bi, a is the real part, while b is the coefficient of the imaginary unit i.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-789c-9fa1-9168d3225b93","description":"Real & Imaginary","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7d65-8508-2b1ee50eb459","description":"True & False","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-710f-a926-a97db61d6ac2","description":"Big & Small","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-76b0-a401-2ccebb99334a","description":"Logical & Intuitive","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7acc-b39d-bd8e2321a371","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which Soviet spacecraft carried the dog Laika into orbit in 1957?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Laika became the first animal to orbit Earth aboard Sputnik 2, but she did not return alive.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7eaa-acb3-680389396914","description":"Sputnik 2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-74c6-b803-f9145981770b","description":"Sputnik 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e2a-b45b-b1133ac3c61e","description":"Vostok 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7ddb-bfef-5f52434e6717","description":"Luna 2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-70bb-b118-38478830cba6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the smallest bird in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Bee Hummingbird is native to Cuba, and females are slightly larger than males.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7039-9c50-183a86656a58","description":"Bee Hummingbird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e9b-9ee8-3a658e66db0f","description":"Pigeon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-76d4-9c76-d2f0f0f65c73","description":"Great Horned Owl","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-76f4-ba52-6b0db9d49d79","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7812-ba1a-daba52cb6647","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What infectious lung disease is known by two letters?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"TB stands for tuberculosis, a bacterial infection that most often affects the lungs and can spread through the air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-700f-8268-431dd8502b6d","description":"TB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-79ad-9155-8a6bead045ac","description":"HF","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-777e-8461-e1cc10b531f6","description":"CC","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-79ff-8225-ce401b264c7f","description":"AK","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-76af-9d44-7690f41cc064","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Venereology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Venereology is the study of sexually transmitted diseases. Its name is related to \u201cvenereal,\u201d a term historically associated with Venus, the Roman goddess of love.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-72d8-8cd2-dfba863ac3d0","description":"Sexually transmitted diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7816-9f2d-52c9e7594153","description":"Vocal sounds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7a3f-b629-780fa3c3625a","description":"Grasshoppers and crickets","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7cf0-a367-83f8f272be7b","description":"Ants","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e7f-b958-3930c3aec0b0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What upward force acts on an object that is immersed in fluid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The buoyant force follows Archimedes\' principle: its magnitude equals the weight of the fluid displaced by the immersed object.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7737-bf23-dc3c5bc75c03","description":"Buoyant force","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-729f-b0e7-9f6ae8dc9bc1","description":"Shear force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7797-9b2b-156168ac1b2c","description":"Viscous force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7518-8576-72ff0b1bc504","description":"Drag force","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7cf2-a0dd-3e8fe3ca2bb6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In laboratory settings, what word is used to refer to the act of stirring or shaking a liquid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Agitating a liquid helps distribute its contents or resuspend settled material; a vortex mixer does this rapidly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-737c-9f3e-9d29bad9acbd","description":"Agitate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c95-a614-a0622a721fe0","description":"Oscillate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-77ab-abb9-2182e7a1a14c","description":"Dilute","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-73e2-ba2f-dea6bf69fb29","description":"Tremble","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7d3d-9c83-dc991f20de3b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In 1898, which noble gas was discovered and named after the Greek word for \'hidden\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Krypton makes up only a tiny fraction of Earth\'s atmosphere, so it had to be isolated from liquefied air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7fcf-a011-aaec5fbbe86d","description":"Krypton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7f79-b2ac-5d13a97b4752","description":"Argon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-747e-b4a0-51c6f56886ef","description":"Helium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7eaa-baca-3984f80df2f8","description":"Xenon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-75c6-91a8-4de03095ae66","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical mercury often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mercury is liquid at room temperature and expands predictably as it warms, making it useful in measuring instruments. Its toxicity has led to safer replacements in many applications.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7ecf-811c-238fd9393814","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c30-9eb3-776c951c7c99","description":"It is used as an ingredient in baking.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-751e-9deb-670d5295744b","description":"It is used as an ingredient in the production of glass, bricks, and ceramics.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7b8a-9fe5-6859c9f756fe","description":"It is used in disinfectants and antiseptics.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7976-b34b-0786b14daddb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of owls?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A parliament of owls is the established collective noun. The same word names a legislative assembly, giving the phrase a stately tone.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c5d-8d85-8f4697d001a4","description":"A parliament","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7310-9b1a-09388c0508cc","description":"A host","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7b7d-8bc1-339c7639cc15","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7dac-b1e3-3b1ac2c62996","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-79fc-8dad-36690e00fbd7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hypnology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Sleep research distinguishes REM and non-REM stages by patterns of brain activity and eye movements.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7bf8-b992-c6d3e855899e","description":"Sleep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7b75-8181-435283fe288c","description":"Radiation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7227-9280-e57723a672dd","description":"Earth materials","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-746a-8742-5da855a996a5","description":"The eyes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-72de-8be4-cfe69afcf2d4","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a young termite?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Termites undergo incomplete metamorphosis, so young hatch as nymphs that resemble small adults.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7093-82a3-48d955dfb68a","description":"A Nymph","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e41-9c78-c4fd2de1388d","description":"An Elver","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-713d-98fc-b95f3be75ccb","description":"A Kitten","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-732a-a456-868bc2e69f17","description":"An Owlet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-76e4-b57b-c94abf82d0d4","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Pathology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Pathology investigates the causes and effects of illness. Pathologists often examine tissue, blood, and other samples to help diagnose conditions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-79da-855b-c8c173e9955b","description":"illness","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7669-a3b8-ff5fc63393f1","description":"the classical Chinese literary masterpiece Dream of the Red Chamber","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7d48-8c58-b600916a1d2e","description":"the practice of escaping from restraints or other traps","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-795b-a91f-6ed224035da2","description":"fermentation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7222-bef5-ebdebbd94d9a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who invented dynamite?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alfred Nobel patented dynamite in 1867, and his will provided for the prizes that bear his name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7a36-90d0-97d115fb2271","description":"Alfred Nobel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7880-8b0b-b0d868fc0da0","description":"Nikola Tesla","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-727c-9a5e-17ce92856d86","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7f32-a4ad-16be818a8ba8","description":"Leonardo da Vinci","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7864-bd45-b8de949b4b36","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the SI unit of pressure?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The pascal is named after Blaise Pascal, a French mathematician and physicist who studied pressure.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7645-9806-c234e2dd490a","description":"Pascal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7042-a6a8-47a7ce709781","description":"Newton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-743d-9312-18d4263134a1","description":"Joule","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7df8-9aec-782a417d84d6","description":"Watt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-796a-be75-971b7089f536","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest species of penguin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The emperor penguin is the largest living penguin and breeds during the Antarctic winter.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c75-b7a3-fd238c32abf5","description":"Emperor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-719e-9236-891973713d86","description":"King","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e4d-ab41-1522a7a5221d","description":"Gentoo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-738f-8333-25018147a29b","description":"Ad\u00e9lie","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-793d-bded-388bf9571ec5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a young mule?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A foal is the young of a horse or donkey. A mule is the hybrid offspring of a male donkey and a female horse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-718b-98ff-0b1b21744522","description":"A Foal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-785d-ada5-65066c5493db","description":"A Cria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-73aa-a3be-ae1bd326661a","description":"A Bunny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7a31-8a59-9e3f2aee3d7a","description":"A Lamb","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-74fb-9f8d-2ed8aa58622c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What name is often used to refer to a type of flying possum?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A glider has a membrane of skin between its limbs that lets it travel between trees without powered flight.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-725c-baee-ade4e1ebe328","description":"A glider","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7cc6-bf15-ecae648b3aba","description":"A leaper","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7313-849e-f22d5c58401c","description":"A flyer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-72c8-88cf-39f70f2713a1","description":"A hanger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c59-bb04-41094085c880","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is dry ice made of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Carbon dioxide is called dry ice because it changes directly from a solid to a gas at ordinary pressure, without melting into a liquid.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-74fa-9dab-1ef8242f1e01","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-740d-847b-0d5c65c86953","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-70a7-8ec4-681f1bbf3913","description":"Oxygen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7bc4-af87-f15080971514","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7b83-b10e-46322f3bac8e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Paleoanthropology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Paleoanthropology uses fossils and archaeological evidence to trace how hominins changed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-74be-a595-f37bb1f71f47","description":"prehistoric people and human origins","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7610-9ab9-70189b6809e2","description":"interactions between organisms and geomorphological processes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7160-876e-850b0d4a5392","description":"study of refuse and trash","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-776e-8a0f-659ca433514d","description":"crime","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e64-bd31-abca6adcb141","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of material is loam?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Loam is earth, typically a fertile blend of sand, silt, and clay that supports plant growth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7572-a925-7cb5455d5238","description":"Earth","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7e1f-a788-c11c6b3fb9ee","description":"Wood","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-70d4-8a1e-475eb0af7a34","description":"Metal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7906-b46b-39a62ad06d62","description":"Rock","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-75db-97a9-ce658c4e6d9c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Metrology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Metrology is the science of measurement; its standards help ensure readings can be compared consistently across laboratories and countries.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7b00-908c-cc117679f1fb","description":"measurement","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-75e9-9ad9-a3176eaa6a97","description":"the relationship of biological or other phenomena to their locations","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7957-9b72-9d6ee3dd3fd5","description":"spiders and their kind","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-77d6-bf04-b0122c232acc","description":"wounds and injuries caused by accidents or assaults and their surgical treatment and repair","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7696-bed2-38536e28493d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which venomous spider is recognized by its hourglass-shaped mark?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Black widows belong to the genus Latrodectus, and their bites can cause painful muscle cramps, though severe outcomes are uncommon.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-713e-b36d-b5ea30917fba","description":"Black Widow","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7480-af48-8a349a28e449","description":"Brown Recluse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7108-bd1a-57e0594853b6","description":"Daddy Longlegs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7925-be1b-03e4112b0df6","description":"Tarantula","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7916-ab00-f4b99ad1ee19","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which substance is quickly absorbed through the walls of the stomach?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alcohol can pass into the bloodstream through the stomach lining, though most absorption occurs in the small intestine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-73a6-9aa2-7aa7d059e933","description":"Alcohol","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-75e3-98fe-6d37220dfc6a","description":"Butter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-778e-8883-7e140327ec27","description":"Olive oil","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7063-9c33-980a081987f2","description":"Ice cream","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7062-8792-017da9e5dd27","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What gives flamingos their pink color?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Flamingos process carotenoids from algae and crustaceans and deposit them in their feathers, giving the feathers their pink hue.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7bfd-aec9-3115641838ad","description":"Pigments from their food","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-739a-a581-a56bb7ad837c","description":"Sunburn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7c35-adc0-476550f28a6b","description":"A pink-pigment gene","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7f31-a24e-48ed2f4b4b60","description":"Minerals in the water","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad53-7a6e-a5b8-3a0e55f03607","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868