ription":"Chimpanzees","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7bdc-9bb4-ac9ca1fb29ec","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which is NOT a source of renewable energy?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Petroleum forms over geological timescales from buried organic matter, so it is finite. Biomass, sunlight, and tidal motion are replenished naturally.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7ac7-b96d-4e181a75ac17","description":"Petroleum","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72a8-9bd0-a953c8ded0ed","description":"Biomass","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7c40-a299-f850138caec0","description":"Sun","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7061-b4fd-0e6ed435760b","description":"Tides","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-795e-ad62-b945015c565f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"If you were travelling at mach 2 how fast would you be travelling?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mach number compares an object\'s velocity with the local speed of sound, so Mach 2 is double that reference velocity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7398-9e09-2c001c3e8a1c","description":"Twice the speed of sound","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-798d-a1e1-8406468517cf","description":"Twice the speed of light","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-778c-9a25-f9cdbf2dd8d0","description":"200 miles per hour","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-77ed-912d-389ebc32332a","description":"2 miles per second","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7100-8b2f-0d7918667f49","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these scientific theories was an improvement over the theory of mechanics by Isaac Newton?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"General relativity extends Newtonian gravity and predicts that massive objects bend light, an effect confirmed by observations near the Sun.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-73d7-8e55-13aec6253bc5","description":"General relativity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-792c-9fdf-57d57835d9a2","description":"Lamarckism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72e1-ab9d-a88893a19476","description":"Maxwell\'s equations","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-705b-bd62-964f3d14dc92","description":"Snell\'s law","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7b14-bbab-58e781a11961","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many neck vertebrae does a giraffe have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Seven is also the usual number of neck vertebrae in humans; giraffes\u2019 vertebrae are simply much longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7744-b716-4e83a2660ae3","description":"Seven","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7915-b9fa-3af1ddd69f73","description":"Fourteen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7b95-93e7-68ef5983a9a9","description":"Nine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7fad-9c68-87b210ad2f95","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7014-9e4d-904d1fd0d963","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word used when one tectonic plate moves under another?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Subduction can create deep ocean trenches and volcanic arcs, and it is associated with powerful earthquakes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7121-ba61-bd20f50ab1c2","description":"Subduction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7f33-8bb9-fdca866cb2c6","description":"Profession","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72dc-89f9-375e97eed1ba","description":"Induction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7b95-948b-db0d8621ab8b","description":"Transgression","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7a16-9679-e849b186000d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where in the body is the smallest human muscle?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The stapedius, the body\'s smallest skeletal muscle, is in the middle ear and helps limit the stapes\' movement in response to loud sounds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-74da-9e2d-358cc4b4a7fe","description":"Ear","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7f86-8492-81500397b91b","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7534-b0e5-547efa80847c","description":"Hand","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7d24-a861-acc0561cfb06","description":"Foot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-77f0-84ee-e58c6d075637","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the specialty of an ophthalmologist?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ophthalmologists are medical doctors who can perform surgery to treat conditions affecting the eyes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-73a0-a89a-15d1b0e0d829","description":"Eyes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7ba9-bc91-107a9c74db79","description":"Testes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7cc3-9ae7-f6209e1ebbd7","description":"Kidneys","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-70f4-9648-6ef0535f394a","description":"Feet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-77f1-95f9-80c2adb80391","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many sides does a heptagon have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The prefix hepta- comes from Greek for seven and also appears in heptathlon, an event with seven disciplines.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7aaf-b8dd-6c98331159a1","description":"7","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7ff7-a87b-8beab59fc8bd","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-79ae-a344-726e8e2018a4","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-763f-ab78-432352a8a06e","description":"9","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72d0-892f-9135f76260f0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hierology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hierology broadly concerns sacred matters, while theology focuses more specifically on God and religious doctrine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7f77-b54e-955154c5d1be","description":"a more inclusive term for theology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7faa-bde6-26b4cb137bbe","description":"the history, languages, and cultures of the Indian subcontinent","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-79ff-9684-3a0f940f1e12","description":"the Sumerians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7cff-9528-484765865c84","description":"crayfish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7263-b856-cade0ea895fb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which gas, produced by bacteria, forms the holes in Swiss cheese?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In Swiss cheese, propionic acid bacteria release carbon dioxide as they ferment, and the trapped bubbles form the characteristic holes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7910-bb27-e329c7535ff7","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72b4-b1e7-fc976e0de549","description":"Oxygen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7506-9ea0-f0f15a22748d","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7837-a2a8-b4968b5ac331","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72cd-a439-8d392298eed2","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of a triangle with two sides of equal length?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"An isosceles triangle has at least two sides of equal length; when all three sides match, it is also equilateral.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e7d-98c9-a10054afc49d","description":"Isosceles triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-77fb-9249-965860120dc9","description":"Equilateral triangle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-72d1-a1e1-c9b76d2b4aed","description":"Scalene triangle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-74ab-b638-6e27e6cc3b49","description":"Rectangle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7fda-8cdc-67b63628d762","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which is NOT part of the water cycle?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Adherence describes molecules sticking to surfaces; percolation, evaporation, and precipitation describe water moving through the environment or changing state.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-792c-9058-ee87b8d5b125","description":"Adherence","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-78e2-afd2-fae78279df92","description":"Percolation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-778f-978c-26003141919d","description":"Evaporation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7300-9793-6423557b8ec7","description":"Precipitation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-74a7-8e72-534628d7a0ef","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the symbol for Iron?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Fe comes from the Latin name ferrum. Iron is also the main metal in steel.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7360-8c0c-f3be31cc301f","description":"Fe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-796f-94b9-0883e5ec73ad","description":"Az","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7809-b56c-61fc8d9606f0","description":"Ri","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-79ca-993f-75afaef22c12","description":"Ir","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7759-b5fd-a8eb3dc8cf82","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which mammal has the longest gestation period of any land animal, at around 22 months?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Elephants usually give birth to a single calf, which can stand and walk soon after birth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7791-a223-7e9d70f1db9c","description":"Elephant","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7818-b936-30784768442c","description":"Tiger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-790d-9537-5ccfab1cdb49","description":"Hippopotamus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-713d-abcd-a282f38a87db","description":"Giraffe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-795f-95e9-d9db60010554","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical sodium chloride often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Sodium chloride is table salt; concentrated salt draws water out of microbes, helping slow spoilage.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7cc6-9778-bb81d1dfcf98","description":"It is commonly used as a condiment and food preservative.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e2c-8fbd-dfebae7cf3be","description":"It is used to relieve pain.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7aee-8f8c-9bbc58065298","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7eb9-89df-f8cfed1cccb2","description":"It is used in nuclear reactors, as a neutron moderator.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-75e9-8bed-77c6df956883","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which plant has bright yellow blossoms that turn into round, fluffy seed heads?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Each dandelion seed has a fine, parachute-like tuft that helps the wind carry it away.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7992-90ab-ade21a94b800","description":"Dandelion","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-74ef-bde1-89a36ac817da","description":"Lily","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7a59-bf0d-2267b04a911b","description":"Aster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7b15-a2a3-6c8d21e4bb9a","description":"Common flax","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7150-bf43-63da92ab2958","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"With which animals is the disease myxomatosis associated?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Myxomatosis is caused by the myxoma virus. Australia used it in the 1950s to reduce rabbit populations, though resistance later increased.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7cf9-b6d4-cd33fa1e0889","de