 the word for a young bird?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A chick is a young bird; a fawn is a young deer, and a kitten is a young cat.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7868-bc71-3849e581a753","description":"A Chick","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e75-b99b-f48457899b01","description":"A Bunny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-792b-89f9-57e51dd0c74a","description":"A Fawn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7dfc-8e19-d4d0ecdbef56","description":"A Kitten","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7129-906c-f0b9b899f063","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Neurology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Neurology is the medical branch dealing with disorders of the nervous system.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-704c-b86e-6b67e2c6555d","description":"The nervous system","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-754e-a514-9712c76406e2","description":"Embryos","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7d7e-8c47-ab79d1130a53","description":"Mollusks","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7bf9-8b07-3521b9b4b9ab","description":"Bones","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e85-8c1b-2e0c7e2fcb7d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many bits are there in a byte?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A byte is conventionally eight bits. The term octet is used when exactly eight bits must be specified, since byte sizes were not always universal.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-70b9-a3f1-0b8b71918c15","description":"8","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7607-ab54-ba831a9e4831","description":"2","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-749b-a401-f926198c3031","description":"4","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7cf9-bb05-fbe4998fd03f","description":"16","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7458-868f-9b26af142ebf","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What kind of animal is a kookaburra?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A kookaburra is a bird in the kingfisher family, and its call sounds remarkably like human laughter.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7d96-92ec-07d7ce6e1e43","description":"Bird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-73ec-96b2-76e298515fa3","description":"Mammal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-78cf-849b-953e2299b963","description":"Fish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7243-a8f9-44e5c6b1b1d1","description":"Reptile","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-78db-9504-7c3f0d583a81","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What process is used when kidneys are not working properly?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Dialysis can clean the blood through a machine or use the lining of the abdomen as a filter.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-70d0-9d27-19a31785bbbc","description":"Dialysis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7400-96f8-bc06c9ea42ee","description":"Chemotherapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7ab0-92f7-57da7a3d20c1","description":"Physiotherapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7b52-8a5c-71f785776691","description":"Radiation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e4c-b416-97cc1e97c524","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is testosterone?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Testosterone is a hormone involved in sexual development and helps support muscle and bone growth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7764-8402-4353f5f10647","description":"A hormone","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-731f-8c22-219ad6983039","description":"A gland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-733a-a6ea-9b9a5925b278","description":"An amino acid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-77a1-9290-1f62981ef62e","description":"A sugar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-73a0-852e-293fd30e5c84","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which web browser wa