swer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7956-9479-9734d6340b8e","description":"7 \u00d7 6 = 42","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7beb-aff1-42e78f940aa8","description":"9 \u00d7 7 = 63","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7978-9551-6b5f01540736","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Coniology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Coniology is the study of atmospheric dust and its effects; its name derives from the Greek word konis, meaning dust.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7aa8-8a4c-3782d5345089","description":"Atmospheric dust and its effects","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7f06-97eb-e8234e4941b6","description":"Life","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7e77-9749-30f756603dde","description":"Human culture","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7da5-9fc6-6d79471b4d86","description":"Dogs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7bfd-877b-39c58cd8483a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the dinosaur that had a large sail-like structure on its back?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Spinosaurus means \u201cspine lizard,\u201d referring to the long spines along its back that supported the sail.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad54-724a-b1e6-f04f11db83f8","description":"Spinosaurus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7fe5-99f8-d1d7576eb905","description":"Triceratops","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7446-be50-9d836a0771ba","description":"Stegosaurus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-7f70-a094-0cd67e05bc33","description":"Diplodocus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad54-750f-b23c-d35a210b97fc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Symbology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Symbology examines how emblems and images convey meaning; heraldry, for example, gives colors and figures on coats of arms particular associations.","alternatives":[{"id":